<%# THE REALIZATION LAB, FRONT DOOR: the kinds already typed, and the form for
    one more. `Lab::Realization`'s header is the design.

    THE FORM IS FOUR PARAMETERS AND SEVEN EXPECTATIONS AND NOT ONE PROMPT FIELD.
    See that header for why a prompt box here would be a second prompt source
    with no baseline. %>
<%= render "lab/styles" %>

<h1>the realization lab</h1>
<p class="nav">
  <%= link_to "&larr; the stories".html_safe, root_path %>
  &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; one room built from a kind of place you type, on a copy of
  a world that is rolled back afterwards
  &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <span class="warn">drawing a sample spends money</span>
</p>

<h2>the kinds</h2>
<% if @kinds.empty? %>
  <p class="absent">(none yet &mdash; type one below)</p>
<% else %>
  <div class="scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>kind</th><th>world</th><th>inside</th><th>danger</th>
          <th>drawn</th><th>judged</th><th>expects</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @kinds.each do |kind| %>
          <tr>
            <td><%= link_to kind.name, lab_kind_path(kind) %></td>
            <td><%= kind.world %></td>
            <td><%= debug_value(kind.inside, absent: "no inside") %></td>
            <td><%= debug_value(kind.danger, absent: "rolled") %></td>
            <td><%= kind.samples.size %></td>
            <td><%= kind.samples.count(&:verdict?) %></td>
            <td>
              <% if kind.declared.empty? %>
                <span class="absent">(nothing &mdash; nothing to score)</span>
              <% else %>
                <%= kind.declared.map(&:name).join(", ") %>
              <% end %>
            </td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
<% end %>

<h2>the agreement</h2>
<p class="note">
  The other direction of the same calibration. The hit rate on a kind's page asks
  whether the model picked what you said it should; this asks whether the
  realization bench's own checks agree with YOU &mdash; a check that fires on a
  sample you called good is suspect, and a sample you called bad that nothing
  flagged is the next check to write. Offline and free: it is read off samples
  already bought, and <code>rake eval:realization_alignment</code> prints the same
  figures with the evidence.
</p>
<p class="note">
  An ELIGIBLE verdict is one that speaks to the check. A sample you called good
  speaks to every check that could be read on it; a weak or a bad speaks only to
  the checks the aspects you ticked name, so a room faulted for its prose is in no
  exit check's denominator. Below
  <%= Story::Scoreboard::MIN_VERDICTS %> eligible verdicts the counts are shown and no
  percentage is.
</p>
<% @agreement_sets.each do |set| %>
  <%= render "lab/kinds/agreement", set: set %>
<% end %>

<h2>a new kind</h2>
<%= render "lab/kinds/form", kind: @kind %>
